$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=bvmusum  LOC_AFTER=?

* The Moebius function sums to the indicator of 1 over the divisors, with the divisor set written as { x e. NN | x || K } (musum).

s1::musum |- ( K e. NN -> sum_ k e. { n e. NN | n || K } ( mmu ` k ) = if ( K = 1 , 1 , 0 ) )
s2::breq1 |- ( n = x -> ( n || K <-> x || K ) )
s3:s2:cbvrabv |- { n e. NN | n || K } = { x e. NN | x || K }
s4:s3:sumeq1i |- sum_ k e. { n e. NN | n || K } ( mmu ` k ) = sum_ k e. { x e. NN | x || K } ( mmu ` k )
s5::fveq2 |- ( k = d -> ( mmu ` k ) = ( mmu ` d ) )
s6:s5:cbvsumv |- sum_ k e. { x e. NN | x || K } ( mmu ` k ) = sum_ d e. { x e. NN | x || K } ( mmu ` d )
s7:s4,s6:eqtri |- sum_ k e. { n e. NN | n || K } ( mmu ` k ) = sum_ d e. { x e. NN | x || K } ( mmu ` d )
s8:s7:a1i |- ( K e. NN -> sum_ k e. { n e. NN | n || K } ( mmu ` k ) = sum_ d e. { x e. NN | x || K } ( mmu ` d ) )
qed:s8,s1:eqtr3d |- ( K e. NN -> sum_ d e. { x e. NN | x || K } ( mmu ` d ) = if ( K = 1 , 1 , 0 ) )
$)
